t\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">makes sense<br /> <br /> and the fledgling recieves a free lesson on Kindred Politics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Its actually litterally not free....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T20:56:13-07:00","id":1142401,"title":"","content":"good point maybe &quot;early&quot; or &quot;effective&quot; is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T20:59:43-07:00","id":1142404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/983363-supernatural-economys-of-barter?p=1142385#post1142385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">saw in one RP the prince decided to forgive an illicit embrace, but decided to demand a boon from Sire and Child alike and wondered why he'd want a boon from the fledgling.</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly he can get away with it. Why not take a free boon without any consequences? Punishing the sire this way is only reasonable. Is the fledgling really to blame for the crime? no, but he's just that an illegally created fledgling, no one (except for the sire) cares. Letting him live for only a boon is allmost merciful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T00:48:45-07:00","id":1142432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/983363-supernatural-economys-of-barter?p=1142385#post1142385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">saw in one RP the prince decided to forgive an illicit embrace, but decided to demand a boon from Sire and Child alike and wondered why he'd want a boon from the fledgling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boons are intangible and if you say you aren't playing the game suddenly you are worthless to anyone who does (The entire Camarilla) If you kill someone that owes a boon, that person will still say they are owed their boon, so it's also protection for the fledgling; anyone who kills them suddenly owes the prince that boon instead.<br /> <br /> (You don't suddenly own boons if you kill someone though)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T08:05:10-07:00","id":1142517,"title":"","content":"Traditionalist Mages use Tass as a kind of effective. Solid Quintessence it's usually an acceptable way of payment for any magical favor you may need (but regular cash or other stuff may do it too, if the mage needs/wants it). Hermetics use boons too.<br /> <br /> Technocratic mages use nothing: Technocracy it's a &quot;job&quot;. You don't &quot;barter&quot; with you boss, you follow your boss orders and then get paid (in this case, a lot). Payment it's in regular money and Tass. Also, if you're efficient in your job and in good terms with the Syndicate, you get to feed your Requisitions Backround, a representation of the trust Technocracy has in your character that allows you to ask for whatever superweapon, resource or personel you think you need to do your job. Technocracy it's tough but fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-21-2017, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T15:15:03-07:00","id":1143606,"title":"","content":"Think a vial of Vampire Blood is enough to qualify as Tass?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T21:39:21-07:00","id":1143668,"title":"","content":"1 Blood Point is worth 1 quintessence; but most Tass doesn't burn up in the sunlight.<br /> It also has a sympathetic connection to the vampire, which is good? for the mage and bad? for the Vampire. Unless the mage drinks it without ripping the quintessence out of it, becoming a ghoul and bonding themselves to the vampire/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T08:43:48-07:00","id":1143802,"title":"","content":"Indeed, vampire blood it's Tass. It's laden with resonances of death,hunger for human blood, and other evil stuff. This fact can increase or reduce it's value. Some mages aren't going to accept payment that's the stuff of evil dark magic...while others would find it even more valuable (the resonance will aid the roll to cast necromantic and/or &quot;vampire-like&quot; stuff).<br /> <br /> Vampires can produce Tass at a rate that may seem too high for Mage economy. Of course vampires versant on the Tremere should know that giving blood to wizards it's not always a good idea... that and the fact that you need a Prime 3 spell or artifact to use it effectively without becoming a Ghoul slave balances this to some extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-25-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T19:54:38-07:00","id":1143950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/983363-supernatural-economys-of-barter?p=1142517#post1142517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocratic mages use nothing: Technocracy it's a &quot;job&quot;. You don't &quot;barter&quot; with you boss, you follow your boss orders and then get paid (in this case, a lot). Payment it's in regular money and Tass. Also, if you're efficient in your job and in good terms with the Syndicate, you get to feed your Requisitions Backround, a representation of the trust Technocracy has in your character that allows you to ask for whatever superweapon, resource or personel you think you need to do your job. Technocracy it's tough but fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you think Requesition and Secret weapons comes into existence? There's definately a level of office politicing in the Technocracy. Favor trading. Building up relationships with more powerful members are your mentor who probably aren't your direct boss but they can lean on them. If you &quot;don't seem like a team player&quot; you sure as hell loose access to shit and people who do favors for people outside direct orders generally tend to get favors in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T06:42:42-07:00","id":1144042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you think Requesition and Secret weapons comes into existence? There's definately a level of office politicing in the Technocracy. Favor trading. Building up relationships with more powerful members are your mentor who probably aren't your direct boss but they can lean on them. If you &quot;don't seem like a team player&quot; you sure as hell loose access to shit and people who do favors for people outside direct orders generally tend to get favors in return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but precisely because of this &quot;barter&quot; isn't the correct word. Barter assumes you set a price, then if that price isn't met you can refuse. Obviously Technocrats socialize, and you may exchange stuff and are encouraged to do good things for others, but because you need to act like &quot;a team player&quot; you can't realy barter because that would imply denying stuff that other people may need fo no reason but your personal gain.<br /> <br /> Secret weapons it's about your social interactions, getting along with the techies to get experimental things that perhaps you shouldn't have. Calling that a &quot;favor economy&quot; a lo Camarilla would be wrong, I think. You want to get along with your workmates and that may mean doing them favors (or not, maybe they just like you), but no authority it's keeping tabs of how many favors you owe, what each favor costs and so on. You can't demand a secret weapon because the techie owes you a favor.<br /> <br /> Requisitions it's more like favors, albeit supposedly amounts to the trust the Technocracy has on your capability of producing results...as defined by the economist convention, and of course the Syndicate likes economy and probably barters with Requisitions, but this also it's vague. The Syndicate doesn't &quot;owe&quot; you Requisitions, Disbursements gives or takes these privileges, having their good will may or may not include doing some &quot;off the charts&quot; favors to them (actually providing money/Qiuint for the Union likely works better than that, Syndicate loves when the investment has tangible returns).<br /> <br /> In the Traditions you may want the assistance of an Euthanatos assasin. The usual method it's to pay the assasin a quantity of Tass (let's say, 10 points) AND argue your point. If you don't have this you usually can't get that help unless you can pull favors (and only the Hermetics have a system to enforce this beyond the accepted social custom of returning favors) or do something to avoid the payment.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200bIn the Technocracy, if you need an assasin and you're paying him out of the grid, you're onto some shady stuff. Totaly likely to happen because Technocracy has more skeletons than closets, but it's not a very &quot;team player&quot; attitude. A &quot;team player&quot; has a specific, mutual, reason to get the kill, and can likely argue her point if it needs to be argued. Obviously, if you've done favors to everyone you're more likely to get your stuff, but this is hardly a &quot;favor economy&quot; where people it's keeping tab on how much they owe you and how much you owe, it's socialization 101.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-26-2017, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T21:59:56-07:00","id":1145443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/983363-supernatural-economys-of-barter?p=1142392#post1142392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Its actually litterally not free....</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so. The Boon owed is payment for the fledgling's continued existence. The <i>Lesson</i>, by contrast, the Prince gives for free.<br /> <br /> In that case, the Prince is being exceedingly generous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T14:48:49-07:00","id":1145637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\