er a year but something came up in a game im in.<br /> <br /> Ideas how to calculate using a Rite or ritual on your behalf?<br /> <br /> is it safe to say a cub can expect to get a set of clothes dedicated within a few days of his firsting as a freebie?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine that. Not in the way that the cub can expect it, but rather that a cunning senior gifts it to start a relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T07:15:29-08:00","id":1274552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/983363-supernatural-economys-of-barter?p=1145443#post1145443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so. The Boon owed is payment for the fledgling's continued existence. The <i>Lesson</i>, by contrast, the Prince gives for free.<br /> <br /> In that case, the Prince is being exceedingly generous.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's how you end up going to the Elizabeth Dane for some Ventrue Princess in a glass tower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T19:09:32-08:00","id":1274649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/983363-supernatural-economys-of-barter?p=1273985#post1273985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it safe to say a cub can expect to get a set of clothes dedicated within a few days of his firsting as a freebie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Other people likely have different experiences, but I have never seen that happen. As an ST, I'd allow it if the PC has the Mentor background or something else that indicates he has someone older and more experienced looking out for him. But I'd not simply give it for free to any PC or NPC. It would have to explained, and simply being a member of the sept is not sufficient in my book.<br /> <br /> Now I would not have the price be very high. It's a common enough thing. But the ritemaster needs to do the work, and spend the Gnosis. He needs to be paid somehow. And the Garou benefiting from it only has so many &quot;slots&quot; available - a homid starting with only 1 Gnosis only gets one set of clothes. Are the ones he has after his First Change really the ones he wants? Especially since most homids change in their young to mid teens and still growing?<br /> <br /> I think if someone did dedicate talismans for a cub, it would much more likely occur right before or right after his Rite of Passage. And there be chiminage exchanged for it - not given for free.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T19:15:50-08:00","id":1274652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/983363-supernatural-economys-of-barter?p=1274049#post1274049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can imagine that. Not in the way that the cub can expect it, but rather that a cunning senior gifts it to start a relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is very important. Exchanging gifts is done to start, maintain, or develop a relationship between Garou (or spirits, or anyone). We are much more used to dealing with a commercial economy, but historically among primitive peoples the primary purpose of gift giving is to maintain and develop relationships. Reciprocal gift giving among friends, and powerful giving gifts to the community to enforce their high social standing and win obedience.<br /> <br /> Such gifts aren't done for charity, or aren't done out of a commerce, but to create a relationship - and with any cub that relationship would be one of a protective superior to a needy inferior and create bonds of obligation.<br /> <br /> That kind of thing either needs to happen in game, or be developed appropriate in a person's backstory. That may not mean it has to take the form of game mechanics (Backgrounds and Merits/Flaws), but it has to be real for the PC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T02:03:36-08:00","id":1275047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/983363-supernatural-economys-of-barter?p=1274652#post1274652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is very important. Exchanging gifts is done to start, maintain, or develop a relationship between Garou (or spirits, or anyone). We are much more used to dealing with a commercial economy, but historically among primitive peoples the primary purpose of gift giving is to maintain and develop relationships. Reciprocal gift giving among friends, and powerful giving gifts to the community to enforce their high social standing and win obedience.<br /> <br /> Such gifts aren't done for charity, or aren't done out of a commerce, but to create a relationship - and with any cub that relationship would be one of a protective superior to a needy inferior and create bonds of obligation.<br /> <br /> That kind of thing either needs to happen in game, or be developed appropriate in a person's backstory. That may not mean it has to take the form of game mechanics (Backgrounds and Merits/Flaws), but it has to be real for the PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly. But way better conveyed, kudos!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}